  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Periodic showers and scattered thunderstorms this \nweekend into early next week.\n\nAfter a fair weather day Friday, conditions will turn more unsettled \nthis weekend and last into early next week. High pressure over the\nregion Friday will slide east, as upper level troughing over \nOntario digs southeastward and eventually closes off over southern\nOntario/southwestern Quebec. An attendant elongated surface low\nwill push a warm front into our region Saturday, followed by a \ncold front Saturday night into Sunday morning. The warm front \nand increasing moisture and modest diurnal instability should \nsupport the development of some showers and scattered \nthunderstorms Saturday afternoon and evening, with a round of \nmore widespread showers and a embedded thunderstorms likely \nfollowing Saturday night into Sunday morning as the cold front \ncrosses our region. A progressively cooler cyclonic flow will \nthen support some additional scattered to numerous instability- \ndriven showers/storms for the rest of Sunday through Monday, \nwith some enhancement from the lakes also becoming likely.",
